{
  "meta": {
    "game": "pokeemerald-based ROM hack (Emerald engine; cosmetic BPRE header). Offsets are VANILLA pokeemerald.",
    "hack_warning": "The hack ENLARGED both save blocks: SaveBlock2 ~0xFE4 (vanilla 0xF2C, +0xB8) and SaveBlock1 ~0x3E14 (vanilla 0x3D88, +0x8C). Insertion points unknown -- offsets after them may be shifted. KNOWN-STALE: the hack's item table (gamedata.json) proves SIX bag pockets (Items/Medicine split), so the vanilla 5-pocket bag layout at SB1 0x560-0x847 does NOT hold in the hack; bag offsets/capacities must be recovered empirically. Verify everything per structs-notes.md.",
    "source": "pret/pokeemerald decompilation, clone at ./pokeemerald",
    "byte_order": "little-endian throughout",
    "alignment": "GBA agbcc uses old ARM APCS: every struct has minimum 4-byte alignment and its size is rounded up to a multiple of 4 (e.g. struct Time occupies 8 bytes, struct Pokeblock strides 8). Offsets below are the true GBA values from the annotated headers, cross-checked by compilation.",
    "ram_pointers": {
      "gSaveBlock1Ptr": "0x03005AD0",
      "gSaveBlock2Ptr": "0x03005AD4",
      "gPokemonStoragePtr": "0x03005AD8",
      "note": "IWRAM pointer addresses for THIS hack (from the rom-fingerprint agent). Blocks are heap-allocated with a random per-load shift; always dereference these."
    }
  },
